From: Termux KMail wallet fix
Subject: kwalletd6: fall back to the configured wallet name when no default collection exists

On a fresh profile ksecretd has no collections, so
org.freedesktop.Secret.Service.ReadAlias("default") returns "/" and
SecretServiceClient::defaultCollection() reports failure. KWalletD::networkWallet()
then replies with the D-Bus error "Failed to query default collection".

Two client classes break on that reply:
  * qtkeychain (used by Akonadi resources, KMail account wizard, MailTransport)
    probes KWallet with networkWallet() and treats the error as "KWallet not
    available", falling back to libsecret on org.freedesktop.secrets.
  * KWallet::Wallet::NetworkWallet() (used by libkgapi for Gmail OAuth tokens)
    returns an empty string, so openWallet("") is attempted.

Before the Secret Service bridge (kwalletd <= KF 6.1x) networkWallet() returned
the configured name unconditionally. Restore that contract: when the default
collection does not exist yet, answer with the configured name so the first
open() call reaches ksecretd and shows the create-wallet dialog.

Upstream reference: invent.kde.org/frameworks/kwallet MR 157 introduced the
error reply (merged 2026-07-28, shipped in KF 6.31).

--- a/src/runtime/kwalletd/kwalletd.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/kwalletd/kwalletd.cpp
@@ -1013,8 +1013,11 @@
     const QString defaultWallet = m_backend->defaultCollection(&ok);
 
     if (!ok) {
-        sendErrorReply(QDBusError::Failed, QStringLiteral("Failed to query default collection"));
-        return {};
+        // No default collection exists yet (fresh profile, ReadAlias("default")
+        // returns "/"). Answer with the configured name, as kwalletd did before
+        // the Secret Service bridge, so that clients can create the first wallet
+        // through open() instead of treating KWallet as unavailable.
+        return KWallet::Backend::networkWallet();
     }
     return defaultWallet;
 }
@@ -1030,8 +1033,8 @@
         const QString defaultWallet = m_backend->defaultCollection(&ok);
 
         if (!ok) {
-            sendErrorReply(QDBusError::Failed, QStringLiteral("Failed to query default collection"));
-            return {};
+            // Same fallback as networkWallet(): no default collection yet.
+            return KWallet::Backend::localWallet();
         }
         return defaultWallet;
     }
